data: {"type":"reasoning-end","id":"tY8Rn6na8sWadnjs","providerMetadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm structuring a concise response: first laying out the lipid panel numbers (LDL up to 131, ApoB 99, non-HDL 167, Lp(a) normal) with the cardiovascular risk estimate, then narrowing down to two or three key actions like the psyllium/oats plan and the statin decision point.\n\nI'll settle on three concrete suggestions — psyllium plus oats, plant sterols (2-3g/day), and flagging a statin discussion with a GP or cardiologist around atorvastatin 10-20mg/day — then wrap up by noting LDL and ApoB should be rechecked at 12 weeks. I'll keep the questions section tight, skipping tangents like ancestry, and since there are no evidence rows to cite, I'll leave the sources section empty.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGNsYXVkZS1vbi1hd3MifQ"}]}}}

data: {"type":"text-start","id":"gen-1791231645-QqWE2eK5tJRd6x8qsl9O"}

data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"gen-1791231645-QqWE2eK5tJRd6x8qsl9O","delta":"Your LDL is 131 mg/dL, up from"}

data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"gen-1791231645-QqWE2eK5tJRd6x8qsl9O","delta":" 117 in December. That is above the 100 limit and well over the optimal under 70. ApoB is 99 against an optimal under 80, and non-HDL is 167 against under"}

data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"gen-1791231645-QqWE2eK5tJRd6x8qsl9O","delta":" 130. Lp(a) is 25, which is fine. The engine puts cardiovascular risk at possible (43 %).\n\nStart with psyllium husk 10 g/day plus about 70 g of oats (3 g beta-glucan) daily for 12 weeks ["}

data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"gen-1791231645-QqWE2eK5tJRd6x8qsl9O","delta":"science]. That should take LDL down roughly 13 mg/dL from the psyllium and about 10 from the oats, so 131 to about 110-118. You can add plant sterols or"}

data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"gen-1791231645-QqWE2eK5tJRd6x8qsl9O","delta":" stanols, 2-3 g/day with a meal [science, A, guideline]. If the repeat numbers are still high, ask a GP or cardiologist about atorvastatin 10-20 mg/day, once daily [opinion]. That dose should lower LDL by"}

data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"gen-1791231645-QqWE2eK5tJRd6x8qsl9O","delta":" about 42 mg/dL, and ApoB should fall from 99 to under 80.\n\nRepeat LDL and ApoB after 12 weeks on the fibre. That result decides the statin question."}

